 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Ask for help and follow a route",
   "texto": [
    "Kan du hjelpe meg? means «Can you help me?». Meg is the form of jeg object: in Spanish it also changes «I» to «me» when it receives the action.",
    "To give a route, you can chain the imperative: Gå rett fram. Følg veien. Vis meg kartt. In many ways, the imperative is built by removing the -e end of the infinitive: å følge → følg."
   ]
  },
